      "text": "To find the number of different starting lineups possible for Coach Grunt's basketball team, we need to determine the number of ways to choose the remaining 3 players from the other 10 players (since Ace and Zeppo are already in the lineup).\n\nWe can use combinations to solve this problem. The number of ways to choose 3 players from 10 is given by the binomial coefficient \\(\\binom{10}{3}\\), which is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 120\n\\]\n\nSo, the number of different starting lineups possible is \\(\\boxed{120}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the number of combinations of 10 players taken 3 at a time\nnum_combinations = math.comb(10, 3)\nprint(num_combinations)\n```",
